      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "INNA ZOU (2) won nicely fresh before being gunned down late at Canberra last time out in easier company. Some sting out of the track looks a big positive for her chances and while she's untested at this distance, there's nothing suggesting she won't run the extra journey. CASINO SHAW (1) drops back in grade after finding them a bit sharp over 1300m at Goulburn last time out. Drawn nicely again today and maps to get every chance. Looks a key player coming back to an easier race. PEARLER (3) won well here two starts ago before turning in a poor one at Nowra last time out. Can bounce back to form under this scenario however. ROSE DIAMOND (4) was just fair last time out at Canberra, but this suits her much better and she can put her best foot forward.",
